WEBVTT

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:05.038
The interview is how Line Select learns what you actually want.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:08.460
Plan on twenty to thirty minutes the first time —

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.533
after that, a new month is a quick check-in.

00:00:12.233 --> 00:00:16.028
Start with your seniority number, if your pack has the list.

00:00:16.028 --> 00:00:19.001
It's only used to estimate what you could hold.

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:25.791
Then the big one: walk it through how you bid, start to finish, in your own words.

00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.914
Type it, or tap the mic and just talk. The more you say, the better your ranking —

00:00:30.914 --> 00:00:34.037
the chips underneath tick off what you've covered.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.119
Tell it whether you commute, and from where.

00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:44.344
Then rate the layover cities in your pack, from Avoid to Love.

00:00:47.718 --> 00:00:51.368
After that it asks questions built from your own story.

00:00:51.368 --> 00:00:57.141
Some are in your words; some show you two real lines or two real trips from your pack —

00:00:57.141 --> 00:01:01.190
tap one to open it in full — and ask which you'd rather have.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:06.963
Near the end you grade a handful of trips, the way you'd size them up on a trade board.

00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:09.551
Skip anything you don't want to answer.

00:01:19.321 --> 00:01:25.287
Last, it reads it all back: your priorities, in order, with what you said next to each one.

00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:28.369
Mark anything that's off, then rank your lines.

